From afc57ea06654f0a93915a89d0d731d29859726e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 06:06:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] swresample/ppc: add AltiVec audio sample format converters

New libswresample/ppc/audio_convert.c with swri_audio_convert_init_ppc
(declared in swresample_internal.h, dispatched from swri_audio_convert_alloc
under ARCH_PPC next to the x86/arm/aarch64 inits). HAVE_ALTIVEC &&
HAVE_BIGENDIAN gated, PPC_ALTIVEC runtime check.

16 kernels, chosen for the conversions a float-decoding player actually
hits on this target (planar decoder output -> interleaved float or s16 AO,
s16 PCM sources -> float internal):
- same-layout (planar->planar or packed->packed, one plane per call):
  int16<->float, int32<->float, int16<->int32
- 2-channel planar<->packed: int32/float no-op pairs (vec_mergeh/l and
  even/odd word permutes), int16 (halfword permutes), and the mixed
  fltp->s16 / s16p->flt / flt->s16p / s16->fltp pack/unpack kernels
- 6-channel planar<->packed for 4-byte samples (FLTP<->FLT, S32P<->S32):
  pairwise merges plus three word permutes per 4 frames

Numerics are bit-exact with audioconvert.c's C converters: int->float is
vec_ctf with the 2^-15 / 2^-31 scale in the instruction (one rounding,
same as (float)i * (1.0f / (1 << N))); float->int scales by 2^15 / 2^31
(exact), rounds with vec_round (vrfin, round-to-nearest-even like lrintf
in the default FP mode -- the ac3dsp float_to_fixed24 idiom, which real
G4/G5 checkasm runs have already confirmed) and converts with the
saturating vec_cts, plus vec_packs for int16, which reproduces
av_clip_int16 / av_clipl_int32 exactly; int16<->int32 are 16-bit shifts.

Alignment: the kernels are registered with in/out_simd_align_mask = 15 (as
the ARM/AArch64 inits do), so swri_audio_convert only calls them when every
plane is 16-byte aligned and falls back to the C converters otherwise; with
its len & ~15 contract that means plain vec_ld/vec_st and no tails. The
library's own buffers are always aligned; only user buffers handed in at odd
offsets take the C path.

Validated under the qemu -cpu 7400 harness: standalone sweep against
scalar references (lengths 16..256, random plus exact-tie and full-scale
inputs, guard bytes) 0 mismatches; checkasm swr_audio_convert (new, two
commits back) shows real ALTIVEC dispatch for every registered pair,
mutation-checked; full suite green. Real-G4/G5 --bench pending.

Not covered (x86 has them, low value here): the 2ch int32<->float and
6/8-channel mixed-type packers, 8-channel packing, and unpack_6ch for
int16.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VY6bhpLDBYqo84Hbm2ewdh
